{
  "rule": "fv3_vorticity_corner",
  "applicable": false,
  "skip_reason": "Layer-A canonical drive of `fv3_vorticity_corner` requires ESS `discretize` to dispatch a cubed_sphere multi-axis composite selector — each stencil row pairs a cell_center selector at axis=ξ offset {-1, 0} with a cell_center selector at axis=η offset {-1, 0} — that EMITS at corner stagger. The multi-axis selector + corner emit is the same ESS extension that holds the other cubed_sphere FV rules' Layer-A back today (see audit dsc-ztvz / F7). The 4-point average (`coeff = 1/4` per row) is the corner-staggered re-aggregation of the cell-mean vorticity emitted by `fv3_vorticity_cellmean`; once the cubed_sphere multi-axis + corner-emit dispatch lands, this stub can be promoted to a hand-pinned canonical contract on a small cN cubed sphere with cross-panel ghost extension exercised at panel-corner boundaries (i,j ∈ {1, Nc+1}).",
  "reference_implementation": {
    "module": "EarthSciDiscretizations",
    "function": "fv_vorticity",
    "path": "src/operators/vorticity.jl",
    "comment": "Imperative reference for corner-staggered relative vorticity, composed with the cell-mean output of `fv_vorticity_cellmean`. Follows Harris et al. (2021) §6 (corner-staggered potential-vorticity flux). Boundary corners draw from ghost-extended cell-mean vorticity supplied by `extend_with_ghosts` in `src/ghost_cells.jl`."
  },
